sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    title HackMatch — US-018: Apply to Join a Team Vacancy — Submission Sequence
    actor Applicant
    participant ReactUI
    participant ExpressAPI
    participant ApplicationService as Application<br/>Service
    participant PostgreSQL

    Applicant->>ReactUI: Apply to an Open vacancy on the platform board
    ReactUI->>ReactUI: Validate optional message at 250 characters
    alt Client validation fails
        ReactUI-->>Applicant: Show field error and preserve message
    else Valid application draft
        ReactUI->>ExpressAPI: POST /api/teams/:teamId/applications without eventId
        ExpressAPI->>ExpressAPI: Verify Firebase token, MFA, active verified PART, and request body
        alt Authentication or validation fails
            ExpressAPI-->>ReactUI: 400, 401, or 403 with explicit code
            ReactUI-->>Applicant: Keep application draft
        else Authorized applicant
            ExpressAPI->>ApplicationService: Submit for teamId, slotId, and message
            ApplicationService->>PostgreSQL: Load applicant, team, Open slot, and requesting-team members
            PostgreSQL-->>ApplicationService: Eligibility context
            ApplicationService->>PostgreSQL: Check duplicate on team and count all platform Pending applications
            PostgreSQL-->>ApplicationService: Duplicate row and global pending count
            alt Express preflight fails
                ApplicationService-->>ExpressAPI: 409 eligibility, duplicate, or quota code
                ExpressAPI-->>ReactUI: No application created
                ReactUI-->>Applicant: Explain failure and preserve message
            else Express preflight passes
                ApplicationService->>PostgreSQL: submit_team_application RPC
                PostgreSQL->>PostgreSQL: Lock applicant and target team
                PostgreSQL->>PostgreSQL: Recheck 250-char message and Open slot
                PostgreSQL->>PostgreSQL: Legacy shadow-event lifecycle, membership, and per-event count checks
                PostgreSQL->>PostgreSQL: Insert Pending Application and owner alert
                PostgreSQL-->>ApplicationService: Application and pendingCountForEvent
                ApplicationService-->>ExpressAPI: Pending Review application view
                ExpressAPI-->>ReactUI: 201 Created
                ReactUI-->>Applicant: Show success and clear message
            end
        end
    end

    Note over ApplicationService,PostgreSQL: Express preflight is platform-wide and team-scoped, but it is not the atomic authority. The current RPC still counts by shadow event_id and gates on shadow-event status and date.
    Note over ReactUI,ExpressAPI: Request payloads reject eventId, but current response DTOs expose eventId and applicantParticipantId. The quota conflict currently maps to HTTP 409 rather than patched HTTP 422.

